hs are inevitable viking's fondness  for killing off its best characters  often winds up not only hurting the  audience but the show itself  several times now vikings has struggled  creatively with its major deaths  the back half of season 3 seemed to  flounder following the murder of  ethelstone for example  and this was made worse because the  death itself felt unearned since it  relied on multiple heal turns prompted  by divine visions to get to that pivotal  moment  conversely in season 4 the death of  ragnar occurred in an immensely powerful  episode which felt both earned and  tragically inevitable  afterwards however the show wandered  around aimlessly for far too  long having lost its focus when it  killed off its main character  in other words while the deaths are  powerful moments in and of themselves  they often leave the show reeling for  all the wrong reasons  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

